# Per-employee env template — read by bin/render-employees-compose.sh.
#
# How it works:
#   1. The renderer scans this file for the line `# === TEMPLATE BEGIN ===`
#      below. Everything ABOVE that line (this header) is for humans
#      reading the example and is NOT copied into seeded env files.
#   2. Everything BELOW is the actual template. The renderer writes
#      it to employees/<login>.env for every employee in
#      employees.json that doesn't already have a file. Two
#      placeholders are substituted at write time:
#
#        __LOGIN__     → the key under "employees" in employees.json
#        __GH_LOGIN__  → that employee's githubLogin field
#
#      Anything else (including ${...} shell expressions) stays literal.
#   3. Re-running the renderer never overwrites an existing
#      employees/<login>.env — fill in real tokens once and they're
#      safe forever after.
#
# To add a new field to all future employee env files, just edit below
# the sentinel.

# === TEMPLATE BEGIN ===

# ---- GitHub bot identity --------------------------------------------------
# Fine-grained PAT for THIS employee's bot account (not the manager's).
# The employee's gh CLI uses this to clone repos, push branches, open
# PRs, and post comments as @__GH_LOGIN__.
#
# Required permissions (fine-grained PAT, scoped to the org):
#   Contents:        Read and write
#   Issues:          Read and write
#   Pull requests:   Read and write
#   Discussions:     Read and write
#   Metadata:        Read (auto-required)
#
# The bot account itself must be a member of N8N_ALLOWED_ORG.
GITHUB_TOKEN=ghs_REPLACE_ME

# ---- Claude Code ----------------------------------------------------------
# Per-employee API key, so each employee's Claude usage shows up
# separately in your Anthropic billing dashboard. Sharing one key across
# employees works too — but you lose the per-employee attribution.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-REPLACE_ME

# ---- Git committer identity ----------------------------------------------
# Cosmetic — shows on commits this employee pushes.
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME=__GH_LOGIN__
GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL=__GH_LOGIN__@bots.onym-n8n.local

# ---- SSH trust ------------------------------------------------------------
# Manager's fan-out pubkey. The manager-agent generates this on first
# boot and prints it via `docker logs onym-manager-agent`. Paste the
# whole single-line ssh-ed25519 string here, then restart this
# employee container so first-run.sh picks it up. Without this set,
# the manager cannot SSH in and dispatch work to this employee.
MANAGER_SSH_PUBKEY=

# Optional: operator admin pubkey for direct interactive SSH to this
# employee (bypasses the manager — lands you at a shell as the `agent`
# user). Useful for debugging or attaching to a tmux session.
ADMIN_SSH_PUBKEY=

# ---- Mac host build delegation (optional) --------------------------------
# Only needed if THIS employee runs iOS / Android NDK builds via the
# host-build-dispatch path. Skip if the employee's specialization is
# pure Linux / web / docs.
MAC_HOST=host.docker.internal
MAC_HOST_USER=your-mac-account
MAC_HOST_PORT=22
